WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.860
Fewer than a dozen work days remain on a Senate-passed ban of death and war contracts. This is Prediction

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:12.400
Markets Daily, episode 59. Journalism and education, never a bet. After that, coin bases

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.300
letter to the cftc, a target date for contracts of its own, and a request that states share

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.220
self-exclusion lists. Then the board, the week's board, and probability waiting. Senators

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:31.820
past S4135, the Death Betz Act on Thursday, November 19 on a voice vote, and the measure

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.020
now sits with the House.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.020
DeFiRate and rg.org both carry the floor account.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.560
A registered entity could not list or clear a contract that expressly references terrorism,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.520
assassination, war, US military operations, or similar activity the CFTC writes into a

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.040
rule, and it could not list a contract that, when listed, is reasonably expected to resolve

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.700
principally because a person has died. John Curtis of Utah and Adam Schiff of California

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:06.520
introduced a wider bill in March, one that would have reached contracts that involve, relate to,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:11.360
or reference those events, or that could be construed as tracking closely to a death.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:17.340
The substitute they passed adds a rule of construction. This statute does not rewrite the law

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.820
on other event contracts, gambling included does not touch the sports contract lawsuits

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:27.760
already in court and does not hand the CFTC power over sports contracts.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:34.420
Mike Leven's companion, HR-7942, has been parked since April in the House Agriculture

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.020
Subcommittee that covers commodity markets and digital assets.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.660
This House term ends January 3, 2027.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.960
Leadership has not said whether S-4,035 gets a slot.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.120
and the amended text was not yet on the Senate website.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.500
Shift's line was that nothing in the act should have any effect on those lawsuits

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.520
and that it should not be read as sports contract authority for the commission.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.500
Curtis said Congress has not and will not give a green light to anyone trying to

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.800
bypass restrictions on contracts against the public interest.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.240
Coinbase in a seven-page letter dated November 18th told the Commodity

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.440
Futures Trading Commission it strongly supports putting sports, politics,

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.160
culture, and weather event contracts inside the swap definition.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:26.060
rg.org has the letter, token post has the same filing, Julia Huckel and David Schaefer

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.840
signed it, and the comment window closed that day.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.700
Coinbase wants the final rule to say qualifying contracts already are swaps, not that they

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.660
become swaps only when the rule starts.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:42.460
It wants the category list left open, and it named Digital Assets, Business Developments,

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:48.380
technology and scientific milestones as further cases with financial or commercial consequences.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.840
Its contrast with a sports book is that an event contract exchange matches buyers and

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.720
sellers, does not set the price, and does not take the other side.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.940
That is Coinbase's argument, not a court finding.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.320
The same letter backs a separate rule that keeps casino-style products out of the swap definition.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.920
Yesterday, Ohio's Attorney General was already with states opposing a sports contract version

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.560
of this idea. The letter now sits opposite a coalition of attorneys general from 43 states

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:22.540
and the District of Columbia who have asked the commission to withdraw the October proposal.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:28.600
In a footnote, Coinbase says it owns the designated contract market Coinbase derivatives LLC.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.520
The Futures Commission merchant Coinbase Financial Markets Incorporated and has newly registered

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:40.520
Coinbase clearing LLC as a derivatives clearing organization. The letter names no launch date.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:46.731
Bloomberg reported Thursday that Coinbase is aiming at the first half of 2027 to list

00:03:46.731 --> 00:03:51.171
US event contracts itself for retail customers and for institutions.

00:03:51.691 --> 00:03:56.911
The timing comes from a person familiar with confidential plans, not from a company announcement.

00:03:57.531 --> 00:04:00.551
Those contracts are offered now through a CalShi partnership.

00:04:01.091 --> 00:04:05.431
Listing them in-house would mean more say over what gets listed and a larger share of

00:04:05.431 --> 00:04:07.071
trading revenue, the report said.

00:04:07.071 --> 00:04:12.031
Back in December 2025, Coinbase agreed to buy the clearing company.

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:16.251
Tony Jemiles start up and said that team would help scale the business.

00:04:16.871 --> 00:04:22.271
In last month's SEC quarterly report, Coinbase tied a rise in other transaction expenses

00:04:22.271 --> 00:04:25.451
