00:08:01.888 --> 00:08:06.328
A stated probability and the weight a person puts on that outcome come apart under ranked

00:08:06.328 --> 00:08:11.528
dependent utility, including prospect theory, and that bend is how it works in the research

00:08:11.528 --> 00:08:12.748
on probability waiting.

00:08:13.408 --> 00:08:15.068
The weight need not equal the chance.

00:08:15.068 --> 00:08:19.888
small stated chances can count for more than their face value. Chances near

00:08:19.888 --> 00:08:24.328
certainty can count for less. The shape estimated again and again is an inverse

00:08:24.328 --> 00:08:31.148
S, concave first then convex. Wu and Gonzalez in Management Science in 1996

00:08:31.828 --> 00:08:35.988
refused to bake that shape into the estimate. Older studies had already

00:08:35.988 --> 00:08:40.608
pointed to an inverse S, but fitting it had required a guest formula for value,

00:08:40.608 --> 00:08:45.248
you, for weights or for both. They gave two preference conditions that are necessary

00:08:45.248 --> 00:08:50.308
and sufficient for concavity, and two's partner for convexity, and that can be checked

00:08:50.308 --> 00:08:55.248
without assuming how value is shaped. The tool was a preference ladder, a run of questions

00:08:55.248 --> 00:09:00.528
that differ only by a common consequence. Those ladders lined up with an S, concave

00:09:00.528 --> 00:09:07.528
up to a probability below 0.40, and convex after that. Non-linearity showed up away from

00:09:07.528 --> 00:09:12.988
the endpoints, zero and one, not only at the edges. The same latter data were fit to

00:09:12.988 --> 00:09:19.008
functions toversky and conumin proposed in 1992, and pre-legged proposed in 1995.

00:09:20.008 --> 00:09:25.628
Abdallahwee, in management science in 2000, split the job and kept it free of a preset formula.

00:09:26.268 --> 00:09:31.248
Utility comes out first, decision waits second, under ranked dependent expected utility,

00:09:31.488 --> 00:09:36.908
and under cumulative prospect theory. For money, utility was concave on gains and convex

00:09:36.908 --> 00:09:42.988
on losses. The weight satisfied upper and lower sub-aditivity and matched earlier parametric

00:09:42.988 --> 00:09:48.608
estimates. In that sample, the weighting function on losses sat higher, more elevated than

00:09:48.608 --> 00:09:54.228
the one on gains. A 2010 paper in Strategic Management Journal argued that strategy scholars

00:09:54.228 --> 00:09:58.768
had inferred the wrong predictions from prospect theory. The value function, it said,

00:09:58.968 --> 00:10:04.148
implies negative risk return links for high performers and positive links for low performers,

00:10:04.148 --> 00:10:06.008
members, the opposite of that literature.

00:10:06.628 --> 00:10:11.868
Isolation means most firm choices should look like mixed gambles, gains and losses together,

00:10:12.308 --> 00:10:15.148
while earlier strategy work had treated them as unmixed.

00:10:15.608 --> 00:10:18.228
And the theory does not spit out one general forecast.

00:10:18.788 --> 00:10:23.228
The forecast depends on parameters and on features of the choice that research had ignored.

00:10:23.708 --> 00:10:28.868
A 2005 review in the annual review of political science noted a different cold shoulder.

00:10:29.448 --> 00:10:32.948
Security scholars in international relations had used the theory a lot.

00:10:32.948 --> 00:10:39.128
While Americanists, comparativists, and political economists mostly had not, that review blamed

00:10:39.128 --> 00:10:44.328
discomfort with behavioral assumptions, not a defect unique to the theory, and left the

00:10:44.328 --> 00:10:48.088
jump from the lab to political decisions in the field as an open problem.

00:10:48.668 --> 00:10:52.488
Hold the market price as a traded price, not as that laboratory weight.

00:10:53.008 --> 00:10:58.328
A contract implying a small probability sits where the 1996 ladders found stated chances

00:10:58.328 --> 00:11:03.408
is overweighted. A price near certainty sits where the curve had turned convex, and the

00:11:03.408 --> 00:11:05.268
weight came in under the stated chance.

00:11:06.008 --> 00:11:10.688
Abdallahweez split between gains and losses says the bend need not match on both sides.

00:11:11.268 --> 00:11:15.828
None of this is a reason to buy or sell anything, and none of it says a venue has already run

00:11:15.828 --> 00:11:17.548
the laboratory curve through its price.

00:11:18.348 --> 00:11:22.668
The screen and the choice experiment are different measurements. That's prediction markets

